# Patterns are matched against the whole context path, so a bare name only
# matches at the top level. Everything that can appear in a subdirectory is
# written as **/<name>.

# Never let a local secret or database into an image layer.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
**/.secrets
**/*.db
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.key
**/*.pem

# ...except the AWS RDS certificate authority bundle, which is the opposite of
# a secret: it is the set of public CAs that sign RDS server certificates, and
# it is what `sslmode=verify-full` checks the app-state database against. It
# has to be inside the image because verification happens in this process, and
# a path on the host is not a path in the container.
!certs/*.pem

# Build/test detritus. Host __pycache__ is worse than dead weight: stale .pyc
# files shadow the source they were built from.
**/.venv
**/venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/htmlcov
**/.coverage
**/*.egg-info
**/dist
**/build
**/node_modules
**/.DS_Store

# The image does not run the test suite.
tests

# Never needed inside the image, and keeping them out means editing the docs or
# the Dockerfile does not invalidate the layer that installs the project.
# Prose is excluded by extension rather than by name so a new document (this is
# how DOCKER.md was added) does not silently start busting the dependency layer
# on every edit. Nothing the build reads is Markdown: pyproject.toml declares no
# readme, hatchling packages only app/, and alembic/README has no extension.
.git
.github
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
**/*.md
fly.toml
# The dev stack and the reverse proxy build/front this image; none of these
# files is ever read from inside it.
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.*.yml
compose.yaml
Caddyfile
